node_modules/
build/
dist/
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env*
!.env.example
# .env.production is committed deliberately. It holds only the PostHog project
# key, which is public by definition — it is compiled into the JavaScript every
# visitor downloads. Ignoring it would hide it from the repository and from
# nobody else, while leaving the build dependent on a dashboard field. Anything
# genuinely secret must never be added to that file: the VITE_ prefix means
# published.
!.env.production
